From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 17:24:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] uml: add Darwin host service implementation

Apply the reviewed final-state topic without intermediate churn.

Each virtual CPU runs on one persistent Darwin carrier thread, and a Linux
task borrows its CPU's carrier instead of owning a host thread. Carrier
lifetime, host-stop wakeup, cross-CPU service, and the hot current-vCPU
lookup live here together.

uml_dir= puts the machine's files directly in the directory it names,
without upstream's <umid>/ level, because Darwin's sun_path holds 104 bytes.
